      "final_answer": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Anya Garcia with user ID anya_garcia_5901. She wants to cancel her flight with confirmation number 3RK2T9 because she's sick and needs a refund. She mentioned she purchased insurance, but the reservation details show that insurance is \"no\". Hmm, there's a conflict here.\n\nFirst, I need to check the reservation details again to confirm. The get_reservation_details response shows insurance as \"no\". The user insists she bought insurance. Maybe there was a mistake during booking? Or perhaps the system didn't record it correctly. \n\nAccording to the policy, if the user has travel insurance and the cancellation is due to health reasons, she's eligible for a refund. But since the system says \"no\" for insurance, I can't proceed. The user needs to clarify or provide proof. But she's insisting she did purchase it. Maybe there's an error in the system. \n\nWait, the policy says the agent must confirm the facts before offering compensation. Since the reservation doesn't show insurance, I can't assume it's there. The user might have made a mistake. Alternatively, maybe the insurance was added later but not updated. But according to the data, it's \"no\". \n\nSince the user's case doesn't meet the cancellation criteria (no insurance, not a business flight, more than 24 hours since booking), I can't process the cancellation. The policy states that if none of the cancellation conditions are met, the agent can't help and must transfer to a human. \n\nSo, I should inform the user that the system doesn't show insurance and explain the cancellation policy. If she still insists, maybe a human agent can review further. But according to the tools, I need to transfer if I can't handle it. So, I should call transfer_to_human_agents with the summary of the issue.\n</think>\n\nThe reservation details show that travel insurance was not purchased for this booking. According to our records, your reservation does not include insurance coverage. \n\nTo cancel this flight, you would need to meet one of the following criteria:\n- Booking made within the last 24 hours\n- Flight cancelled by the airline\n- Business class reservation\n- Travel insurance coverage with a qualifying reason\n\nSince your reservation does not include insurance and the booking was made more than 24 hours ago, I cannot process this cancellation request. Would you like me to transfer you to a human agent to discuss further?",
